1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,035
Everyone posts their NeurIPS acceptances.

2
00:00:03,035 --> 00:00:05,348
Nobody posts how many were rejected.

3
00:00:05,698 --> 00:00:13,267
Of the five top AI conferences, only ICLR
publishes its rejections. Since 2020,

4
00:00:13,267 --> 00:00:20,165
26 lecturers and researchers in Vietnam
sent 61 papers to ICLR in total;

5
00:00:20,165 --> 00:00:22,273
only 13 were accepted.

6
00:00:22,623 --> 00:00:27,650
This year they submitted to NeurIPS again,
and 33 papers were accepted.

7
00:00:27,650 --> 00:00:29,632
If the odds are like ICLR's,

8
00:00:29,632 --> 00:00:33,810
behind them are about 60 to 120
papers that did not get in.

9
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:36,820
And that is only people
with an accepted paper.

10
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:39,876
Those who submitted but have
none yet are not counted,

11
00:00:39,876 --> 00:00:42,196
so the real number of attempts is higher.

12
00:00:42,546 --> 00:00:45,668
And who writes the accepted papers?

13
00:00:45,668 --> 00:00:49,682
Of the 79 since 2020
with known affiliations,

14
00:00:49,682 --> 00:00:56,817
only 35 have a first author from the
lecturer's university and only 25 have most

15
00:00:56,817 --> 00:01:01,187
authors there,
while 31 have most authors abroad.

16
00:01:01,537 --> 00:01:04,907
A paper has 5.4 authors on average,
23 at most.

17
00:01:04,907 --> 00:01:08,923
One accepted paper is good
news for many people at once,

18
00:01:08,923 --> 00:01:12,078
so everyone on it can
say they have a paper.

19
00:01:12,428 --> 00:01:17,359
Rejections still outnumber acceptances,
even for people who already have papers.

20
00:01:17,359 --> 00:01:19,146
Students without a paper yet:

21
00:01:19,146 --> 00:01:20,871
don't be hard on yourselves.

22
00:01:20,871 --> 00:01:22,597
Full data at the link below.
